<description>&lt;p&gt;Rebel forces and government troops continue to clash near the Uganda border, killing one and wounding three, while similar fighting in Greater Tonj sees UNMISS patrols protecting civilians. Communal violence has forced 15,000 civilians to flee Gbudwe and 27,000 displaced in Upper Nile as rival groups battle in Lakes state, prompting the detention of 16 community leaders and the launch of peace talks in Tonj East. IGAD is probing the Bentiu attacks, and a drone strike on a market in the disputed Abyei region killed 73 people, according to Addis Standard. The UCDP recorded 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxON3VmS1doLVpDWU5SUDlBY3VCbWdZUzZYUWtlZmM1MHUyYU8zWHpZYmFzXzZlVEphN0JyRTZrZjZnU0RROTBZMVpxSzNfdFBXYXdLaUo3TVd1YWstVGlQdXhEYTlNTGJoWExzb1pJaHJWQWJKMENGbU94ZzUtbjhJQnhPSVAtY0dhdnpsaklYcE1qTkhrZXVjdHhNQWlsMDJnYkpGcXJ6RVpOSkFtclNFLQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Uganda Radionetwork&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Africa.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiU0FVX3lxTE1LOVBrN0RVU3dtcFVFZVp4TzNDQklKZ2VSSEEtOGRIN2xxcC0xOWpTOFZ0Tkgwam9JZmhyTG1sOURMVXB0ZjRkY1hZUGhzNHFJZnQ4?oc=5&quot;&gt;Apa.az&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiUkFVX3lxTE9vSVBSWjJMX1hFVHZPcmNiOW5uREpxZUJJci1yQVdrWmpOWDBIMVY5aXVNVzR3MV9PRzJqUl9hME5jcHNVVzBZQmhkZGlWcERhTEE?oc=5&quot;&gt;Addis Standard&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiogFBVV95cUxQc3d0SGg2QnRBdkZyNTNFVExOVmsxN09PVEpleEZHek0taWVpYVc0VDZlcUx2cmtPMURpSzRXb0dSbTRQUmIzMmt3dXdfZXN2RHZvZ050bUNMNmhUc21MREF0NUx2eFF1MDQ5SlJIb3JfaDdUbmRJMlBJVlBidG1ueHVoOUlkakJ3WmFza2M1X0paM0lObDEtdXZHaFV1bFBIRlE?oc=5&quot;&gt;Radio Tamazuj